TITLE: YGGDRASIL A49 / T10A — Cooperative-Core Challenge-Phase Periphery Control
DATE: 2026-09-22
STATUS: PREREGISTERED MACRO-ORGANIZATION EXPERIMENT / NON-CANONICAL
TRACK: YGGDRASIL TRAINING T10A / APPLICATION-A
PARENT CORE: A45 ECHO_PHASE
RECOVERY ROBUSTNESS PARENT: A48
PERIPHERY DONORS: A41 / A42
BRANCH: dg1a-ar

WHY A49 EXISTS

A41 proved:

a surviving committed core
can suppress nearby adverse recruitment.

But exclusion alone
did not preserve enough
favored committed population
through the adverse burst.

A42 proved:

a surviving committed core
can actively recruit nearby U cells
toward its own side.

But active recruitment
and simple push-pull
were tested on the weaker
A40-era core.

At adverse-burst end
the favored side still collapsed
to roughly 25-29%.

A43 then established
margin-weighted cooperative reinforcement
as the first mechanism
to materially change
the macro attractor
while preserving reversal.

A45 added
one-epoch cooperative continuity.

The post-A45 phenotype
is no longer primarily
wrong-side capture.

The hard 5:3 cases mainly show:

favored majority
-> unresolved
-> favored majority.

A48 then established
that repaired G5 recovery
is a reproducible moderate aid,
not a transformative mechanism.

Therefore A49 returns
to the macro organization question:

can the now-surviving cooperative core
control nearby periphery turnover
during challenge strongly enough
to preserve favored participation
through the adverse burst?

This is NOT
a rerun of A42.

The causal substrate
has changed materially.

A49 CORE SUBSTRATE

Use A45 ECHO_PHASE
exactly as the parent dynamics.

Preserve:

A36 ecology;

A40 signed temporal state;

A43 margin-weighted cooperative reinforcement;

A44 local
SUPPORT / CHALLENGE / NEUTRAL
committed-cell mode;

A44 support-gated
active margin recruitment;

A45 one-epoch,
non-recursive cooperative echo.

Do NOT include
A46/A48 G5 recovery
in the A49 primary.

Reason:

A48 classified G5_FULL
as a reproducible moderate,
optional recovery aid.

A49 must isolate
the macro periphery mechanism
without recovery-layer confounding.

No refractory rule changes.

No A37 lineage state exists.

F49 FREEZE

Let the exact A49
implementation freeze commit be:

F49.

No real A49 world,
population outcome,
or scientific result
may be derived before F49 exists.

WORLD SHAPE

384 fresh post-F49 trials.

48 contexts x 8 replicas.

48 cells.

48 epochs.

Environmental families
remain structurally identical
to A45/A48.

COMMON-RANDOM DESIGN

All A49 arms within each D family
use the same inherited
A45 ECHO_PHASE
stateless action-random identity.

Worlds,
sensor noise,
heterogeneity,
and inherited event salts
are shared.

A49 periphery transformations
are deterministic.

Thus treatment/control
differences are causally isolated.

SURVIVOR-CORE TIMING

Preserve A42 timing
adapted to the A45 parent:

1. capture B_pre;

2. update signed B;

3. execute H release;

4. execute committed-state
A45 cooperative-echo
defection decisions;

5. freeze
the surviving committed core;

6. classify every surviving
committed cell's
existing A44 local mode;

7. compute challenge-core
periphery fields;

8. execute U recruitment.

The challenge field
reads:

surviving committed identity;

existing local mode;

and,
where needed,
beginning-of-epoch B_pre.

No future evidence.

No global environment phase.

No context identity.

FIELD RADIUS

Use exactly:

R_core = RECRUIT_R = 3.

No new radius exists.

CHALLENGE OCCUPANCY FIELD

For eligible U cell i:

Q_C_ch_occ(i)

=

mean over radius 3
of:

1[
state_j = C

AND

mode_j(C) = CHALLENGE
].

Q_S_ch_occ(i)

=

mean over radius 3
of:

1[
state_j = S

AND

mode_j(S) = CHALLENGE
].

The center position
contributes zero
for an eligible U target.

Normalization remains
the same radius-3 mean
used by A41/A42 occupancy fields.

No gain,
offset,
threshold,
or distance kernel.

A45 PARENT RECRUITMENT

Let:

lambda_C_parent;
lambda_S_parent;
lambda_H_parent

be the exact A45
recruitment intensities
for the current U cell.

These already include
A44 support-gated
active margin recruitment
when locally supported
committed veterans exist.

A49 does not alter
that support behavior.

CHALLENGE OCCUPANCY EXCLUSION

CH_OCC_EXCLUSION:

lambda_C'
=
lambda_C_parent
*
(1 - Q_S_ch_occ).

lambda_S'
=
lambda_S_parent
*
(1 - Q_C_ch_occ).

lambda_H'
=
lambda_H_parent.

Interpretation:

locally challenged
surviving C veterans
make nearby S recruitment harder;

challenged S veterans
make nearby C recruitment harder.

This is a challenge-gated
version of A41's
strongest safe local fence.

CHALLENGE ACTIVE OCCUPANCY RECRUITMENT

CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY:

lambda_C'
=
lambda_C_parent
+
ETA * Q_C_ch_occ.

lambda_S'
=
lambda_S_parent
+
ETA * Q_S_ch_occ.

lambda_H'
=
lambda_H_parent.

Frozen:

ETA = 1/2.

No new gain exists.

Interpretation:

a surviving veteran core
continues to recruit
nearby uncertain cells
toward its own side
even while that core
is locally under challenge.

This is the strongest
safe A42 magnet
placed on the stronger
A45 core substrate.

CHALLENGE PUSH-PULL

CH_PUSH_PULL composes
the two challenge transformations.

For C:

lambda_C'
=
(
lambda_C_parent
+
ETA * Q_C_ch_occ
)
*
(1 - Q_S_ch_occ).

For S:

lambda_S'
=
(
lambda_S_parent
+
ETA * Q_S_ch_occ
)
*
(1 - Q_C_ch_occ).

lambda_H'
=
lambda_H_parent.

No third field.

No new parameter.

No post-result gain tuning.

ARMS

Exactly eight arms.

D2:

D2_BASE_ECHO_PHASE;

D2_CH_OCC_EXCLUSION;

D2_CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY;

D2_CH_PUSH_PULL.

D3:

D3_BASE_ECHO_PHASE;

