PRIMARY PHENOTYPE

A49 does not define success
as simply lowering
the inherited oscillator label.

The primary macro failure
after A45 is:

loss of favored majority
into unresolved states
during / after repeated challenge.

A49 therefore measures
majority continuity
and burst-end organization directly.

5:3 BURST-END COMPOSITION

At every 5:3 adverse-burst end,
report:

favored committed fraction;

adverse committed fraction;

U fraction;

H fraction;

FC fraction;

FS fraction;

total refractory fraction;

total unresolved fraction;

majority label.

For each arm report:

mean burst-end favored fraction;

median burst-end favored fraction;

fraction of burst endpoints
with favored majority;

fraction unresolved;

fraction adverse-majority.

MAJORITY-CONTINUITY METRICS

For 5:3 report:

favored-to-unresolved transitions;

unresolved-to-favored transitions;

unresolved episode count;

mean unresolved episode duration;

median unresolved episode duration;

mean favored-majority recovery latency;

recovery-never count.

Retain the inherited oscillator metric
for lineage comparability only.

CHALLENGE TURNOVER METRICS

At every 5:3 adverse-pulse epoch,
for every eligible U cell,
record:

Q_C_ch_occ;

Q_S_ch_occ;

base parent lambda_C;

base parent lambda_S;

transformed lambda_C;

transformed lambda_S;

whether recruitment fired;

joined state.

Relative to the long-run favored side,
report:

favored recruitment rate
inside radius 3
of challenged favored veterans;

adverse recruitment rate
inside that radius;

H recruitment;

no recruitment;

the same outside radius.

For exclusion arms report:

mean opposing-lambda suppression.

For active arms report:

mean same-side lambda increment.

CORE-SUBSTRATE DIAGNOSTIC

At every 5:3 adverse-burst onset
freeze the favored committed cohort.

Report:

pulse-onset favored fraction;

epoch-1 core persistence;

epoch-2 persistence;

epoch-3 persistence;

burst-end favored fraction.

A49 must distinguish:

periphery turnover improvement

from:

additional committed-core persistence.

A49 periphery rules
must not directly modify
committed-cell defection.

PUSH-PULL SYNERGY

For each D family,
evaluate paired 5:3 burst endpoints.

Define a BASE LOST-MAJORITY endpoint:

BASE majority
at adverse-pulse onset
is favored,

but at burst end
BASE majority is not favored.

A PUSH_PULL-ONLY RESCUE occurs iff:

the endpoint is
BASE LOST-MAJORITY;

CH_OCC_EXCLUSION
also lacks favored majority;

CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY
also lacks favored majority;

but

CH_PUSH_PULL
retains favored majority.

Report:

BASE lost-majority endpoints;

rescued by exclusion;

rescued by active recruitment;

rescued by push-pull;

rescued only by push-pull.

This is the primary
macro synergy signature.

A49 MACRO INFORMATION GAIN

TRUE iff at least one
non-BASE arm satisfies all:

1. mean 5:3
burst-end favored committed fraction
is at least 5 percentage points
higher than paired BASE;

2. 5:3 favored-majority
burst-end frequency
is at least 20 percentage points
higher than BASE

OR

favored-to-unresolved transitions
are reduced at least 25%;

3. direct favored-to-adverse
majority flips = 0;

4. adverse-majority entries
do not exceed paired BASE;

5. 6:2 oscillator
does not exceed paired BASE;

6. balanced false-majority <=10%
and does not exceed paired BASE;

7. reversal acquisition >=80%;

8. median old-majority loss <=4 epochs;

9. aggregate service >=95%
of paired BASE;

10. all integrity probes pass.

A49 PUSH-PULL SYNERGY

TRUE iff CH_PUSH_PULL:

1. satisfies
A49 MACRO INFORMATION GAIN;

2. has higher
5:3 burst-end favored fraction
than both single mechanisms;

3. has higher
5:3 favored-majority
burst-end frequency
than both single mechanisms;

4. produces at least
10% PUSH_PULL-ONLY RESCUES
among BASE lost-majority endpoints;

5. remains safety-clean.

A49 QUALIFICATION

D2_CH_PUSH_PULL
or
D3_CH_PUSH_PULL
is A49-QUALIFIED iff all are true:

1. mean 5:3
burst-end favored committed fraction
>=50%;

2. at least 50%
of 5:3 adverse-burst endpoints
retain favored majority;

3. favored-to-unresolved transitions
are reduced at least 50%
versus BASE;

4. mean unresolved episode duration
is at least 25% lower
than BASE;

5. direct favored-to-adverse flips = 0;

6. adverse-majority entries = 0;

7. 6:2 oscillator = 0%;

8. balanced false-majority <=10%;

9. reversal acquisition >=80%;

10. median old-majority loss <=4 epochs;

11. aggregate service >=95%
of BASE;

12. at least one
PUSH_PULL-ONLY RESCUE exists;

13. all integrity probes pass.

RECOVERY-LAYER BOUNDARY

A49 does not
use G5_FULL.

A49 does not
change refractory timing.

A49 does not
change the A45 echo.

If A49 demonstrates
macro information gain,
a later experiment may test
whether the parked G5_FULL
recovery aid adds independently.

No such composition
is allowed inside A49.

FAILURE ATTRIBUTION

If CH_OCC_EXCLUSION
locally suppresses adverse recruitment
but macro continuity does not improve:

the fence remains locally real
but is not the remaining bottleneck.

If CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY
raises challenged-core
favored recruitment
but macro continuity does not improve:

additional challenge recruitment
is still too weak
or too late.

If both single mechanisms improve
but PUSH_PULL does not exceed them:

the periphery controls are additive
or interfering,
not synergistic.

If PUSH_PULL improves turnover
but favored majority still collapses:

the unresolved mass
is dominated by cells
that are not recruitable U,
consistent with refractory/H occupancy
remaining the limiting reservoir.

If PUSH_PULL preserves majority
but reversal or balanced safety fails:

challenge-phase turnover control
is too persistent or too indiscriminate.

If all three treatments
show little local effect:

the surviving challenge-mode core
is too sparse
to drive a meaningful field.

